ual Neutral Athlete (AIN) but, as a supporter of President Putin and the Russian invasion of Ukraine, the International Olympic Committee did not declare him neutral, and he was not invited to the Games. As a result, the favorites in Paris were the podium finishers of the last World Championship: Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144219"} "Simone Alessio"] " (gold), the US American " [:a {:href "/athletes/155049"} "“CJ” Nickolas"] " (silver), and Egypt’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103312"} "Seif Eissa"] " (bronze)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In testament to the sport’s unpredictability, these top contenders failed to advance to the finals. In the final bout, Tunisia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/155043"} "Firas Katoussi"] " defeated Iran’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/155015"} "Mehran Barkhordari"] " in two rounds, scoring 4-2 and 5-1. Katoussi’s win was Tunisia’s first Olympic taekwondo gold. Simone Alessio and Denmark’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/154992"} "Edi Hrnic"] " won the bronze medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib/Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "606"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/155043"} "Firas Katoussi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUN.png"}] "TUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "608"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/155015"} "Mehran Barkhordari"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "614"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/154992"} 